{"_id":"68a736428ec3d8323af2043f","nodeId":"E88tHQvARkHURZwGaO02l","roadmapSlug":"typescript","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:45.916Z","description":"# Pick\n\n`Pick` is a utility type that constructs a new type by selecting a set of properties from an existing type. You specify which properties you want to include in the new type using their keys. This is useful when you need a subset of properties from a larger type definition.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Pick<Type, Keys>","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/utility-types.html#picktype-keys","_id":"69a965b0ff229973532439b1"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T11:14:56.641Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041649f","title":"Scrimba - Learn TypeScript","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com/learn-typescript-c03c?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/typescript/content/E88tHQvARkHURZwGaO02l.md"}